  "answer": "The TMRS global custody RFP uses four weighted criteria to evaluate respondents:\n\n| Evaluation criterion | Weight |\n|---|---:|\n| Scope affirmation, servicing approach, and institutional credentials | 25% |\n| Core and value-added services and technology platforms | 40% |\n| Quality of response and additional evidence of capability | 10% |\n| Competitiveness and reasonableness of economics | 25% |\n\nThe economics criterion considers fees **relative to service quality**, not simply the lowest price. TMRS may also account for estimated transition costs and risks. Source: *TMRS Global Custody and Related Services RFP*, Section V, p. 22.",
